course: dictionary
lesson: 13206
title: Funds: money with a purpose
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Funds is a word about money. Look at the words around it: «The school is raising funds for a new playground.» Raising means collecting, and a playground costs money, so funds must mean money that people collect for a purpose.
explain: Look at the ending too. Funds ends in s, and a fund is one pot of money. «Our class is short of funds for the trip.» Short of means not having enough, so funds here means the money the class needs.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «The school is raising money for a new playground» still makes sense, so funds means money. Context and a quick swap help you work out new words.
fact: Funds means money that is available to spend, especially for a special purpose.
fact: A fund is an amount of money saved or collected for a special purpose, as in «a holiday fund».
fact: As a verb, «fund» means to pay for something, as in «The council funds the library».
fact: Fundraising means collecting money for a purpose, for example with a bake sale or a fun run.
fact: «A fund of stories» means a large supply of stories.
exercise: «The school is raising funds for a new playground.» What are funds here? | Bricks for a wall | Stories told by teachers | *Money collected for a purpose | A kind of playground game
exercise: «The council funds the library.» What does funds mean in this sentence? | Paints its walls | Closes it on Sundays | *Pays for it | Visits it every day
exercise: «Our class is short of funds for the trip.» What does short of funds mean? | Has too many trips planned | Is very tall | Is saving for a holiday | *Does not have enough money
test: «Grandma has a fund of funny stories.» What does a fund of stories mean? | A short book of stories | *A large supply of stories | A story told by a dog | A lost box of stories
test: The club had £20 in funds and spent £8. How much funds are left? | *£12 | £20 | £28 | £8
exam: A fund is an amount of money saved for a special purpose. Which one is an example of a fund? | *a holiday fund | a fun run | a playground | a bake sale
